  "published": "2026-10-23T05:49:11.01Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Added: The first publication of the package, with the interfaces of 3,339 messages, their components and choices. It was prepared in a monorepo as `BeneficialStrategies.Iso20022.Interfaces` and never published under that name; it is now `BeneficialStrategies.Iso20022.Messages`, in its own repository with its history, and is versioned and released independently of the other packages. The namespaces are unchanged.\nAdded: Versions have three parts, `design.breaking.compatible`: the first changes with a redesign, the second with a change that breaks existing users, the third with every other change. This is not Semantic Versioning.\nAdded: Tests that read the assembly alone and say what every interface must be (one kind marker, get-only properties, an XML tag on every member, a unique identifier for every message, choices with their variants), and that the Factory builds one message of every business area.\nAdded: The README is the package README, and its examples are projects under `examples/` that are built and run against the packed package.",
